---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import sources from '../data/sources.json';
import provenance from '../data/provenance.json';
import content from '../data/content.json';
const retrieved = new Date(provenance.retrievedAt).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' });
---
<Shell title="Sources & methodology" active="sources"><article class="prose"><span class="eyebrow">Evidence and editorial choices</span> <h1>Sources & methodology</h1> <p>{content.methodology}</p><h2>What this app quotes</h2><p>Events cite the UNESCO World Heritage Centre and the Metropolitan Museum of Art. Their named records support the displayed dates at their actual precision. The app quotes no Quran text, commentary or hadith. Land shapes are public-domain Natural Earth data, bundled locally.</p><h2>What is editorial</h2><p>Event summaries are original and concise. Century bands are editorial filters; exact years and construction ranges keep the precision given by the cited institution. None of it is a ruling or an opinion from quran.ai, Quran.com or Quran Foundation, and no independent scholarly review is claimed.</p><h2>Limits</h2><p>The events are a selection, not a complete history. The map is regional orientation without political borders, and no Quran verse is presented as evidence for a later historical date.</p><h2>Snapshot and reuse</h2><p>Canonical snapshot retrieved on {retrieved}. Source records, checksums and edition names ship with the project. Original application code is MIT licensed. DM Sans, Newsreader and Amiri are hosted locally under the SIL Open Font License, with their licence files included.</p><p class="micro">Snapshot SHA-256: <code style="overflow-wrap:anywhere">{provenance.snapshotSha256}</code><br />App content SHA-256: <code style="overflow-wrap:anywhere">{provenance.appContentSha256}</code></p><h2>References used in this app</h2><p>{sources.length} linked sources. Each opens the source provider in a new tab.</p><ul class="source-list">{sources.map(source=><><li><a href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{source.label} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a> <small>{source.kind}{'note' in source && source.note ? ` · ${source.note}` : ''}</small></li>{' '}</>)}</ul><div class="actions top-gap"><a class="button" href="/">Return to the activity <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a> <button class="button secondary" data-print>Print source notes</button></div></article></Shell>
